ces, copied menus and accelerator tables, basic control state, actual framebuffer drawing/text, pointer/edit input, deadline-backed timers, focus/capture, disabled-owner modality, native visible-window admission and teardown. A strengthened 21-lifetime test preserves desktop focus/selection during blocked owner clicks, routes keys to the enabled modal and refuses the wrong context menu. Thirty-two nested windows draw the deepest child correctly. GUI instruction faults release owned resources and allow subsequent original console use.\n\nThe exact prepared VMware ZIP installs on its blank growable 20-GiB SATA disk, starts the installed desktop with the ISO retained, installs the supported original MSI, opens/moves/closes the actual original file-manager window and starts twice from disk alone. All shipped devices remain enabled. This uses authenticated loopback guest input, with the existing VM inventory unchanged. UEFI, Secure Boot off and the supplied settings define this named virtual scope.\n\nAll 47 matching native groups and 8 supporting host groups pass. Earlier process/thread/TLS/exception, Unicode files/sharing/locks, persistent registry, environments, metadata, cancellation and ownership regressions run on the same frozen candidate. The supported original 7-Zip console/MSI lifecycle includes all 106 payload hashes, archive/extraction, removal and reinstall. [Native acceptance](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/58bce09a55b3336ba87f1451880f9a93d4e1367e/evidence/M14/4/acceptance-results.json), [resource observations](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/58bce09a55b3336ba87f1451880f9a93d4e1367e/evidence/M14/4/resources.json).\n\n## Resource scope\n\nFixed desktop state is 557,692 bytes, 176 more than M14.3 in that component. The original initial-window profile peaks at 469 group-owned pages (1,921,024 bytes), including the GUI allocation. Steady GUI storage is 23 pages, including eleven drawing pages. A single declared shared-format cache page remains after first use; repeated closes add zero pages. Both guest CPUs halt during observed message waits. Framebuffer storage is separate. Dispatch quanta are not measured CPU time, and these component values are not total OS RAM or complete archive-task performance. **M14.15 remains the mandatory whole-system CPU/RAM/storage optimization gate.**\n\n## Important limits\n\nThe 7-Zip GUI toolbar/menu, folder-navigation and archive tasks are not complete in this stage. Basic toolbar labels can be cramped; full control/drawing appearance follows in M14.5. Use the supported native frontend console archive actions for the qualified archive tasks. The initial Network/root labels come from the original application and do not establish Windows network-share support.\n\nNotepad++ and SumatraPDF remain inspection-only. Firefox is a verified optional installer download; installation and execution remain unavailable. Reusable MSI, original EXE installers, richer runtime families, complete original-app scenarios and final optimization remain the ordered M14 gates. Windows x86 follows in M15; Win16/DOS follows in M16. No universal hardware, GPU gaming, unlimited uptime or faster-than-Windows claim is made.\n\n[Installation](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/58bce09a55b3336ba87f1451880f9a93d4e1367e/docs/handbook/install-m144.md), [first day](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/58bce09a55b3336ba87f1451880f9a93d4e1367e/docs/handbook/first-day-m144.md), [Windows tasks](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/58bce09a55b3336ba87f1451880f9a93d4e1367e/docs/handbook/windows-m144.md), [window ownership](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/58bce09a55b3336ba87f1451880f9a93d4e1367e/docs/architecture/messages-m144.md), [resources and limits](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/58bce09a55b3336ba87f1451880f9a93d4e1367e/docs/architecture/resources-m144.md), [stage record](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/58bce09a55b3336ba